<item>
            <title>[LU-20891] lnet: lnet_peer_set_primary_nid() publishes a primary NID before the add succeeds</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20891</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Problem&lt;br/&gt;
lnet_peer_set_primary_nid() writes a new lp_primary_nid before lnet_peer_add_nid() runs. If the add fails, the function writes the old value back. A reader with only the net lock can see this transient NID. lnet_parse() can then stamp msg_initiator with that NID, and LNetPrimaryNID() can return it.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Environment&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master at 550451c0e4 and earlier.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Any node with lock_prim_nid=0, or a peer without LNET_PEER_LOCK_PRIMARY.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Reproduction&lt;br/&gt;
Source analysis only. We did not reproduce the failure.&lt;br/&gt;
1. Configure a peer with lnetctl, so that it has LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED and no LNET_PEER_LOCK_PRIMARY.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Let a ping reply from that peer report primary NID B, where B is another NID of the same peer.&lt;br/&gt;
3. lnet_peer_data_present() calls lnet_peer_set_primary_nid(lp, B, flags). flags has no LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED.&lt;br/&gt;
4. The function writes B under lp_lock. lnet_peer_add_nid() returns -EPERM, and the function writes the old NID back.&lt;br/&gt;
5. A lookup between steps 3 and 4 returns B.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Analysis&lt;br/&gt;
The writers of lp_primary_nid hold lp_lock. Readers such as lnet_peer_primary_nid_locked() hold the net lock only. The window lasts from the first write to the restore. It recurs on each discovery round of such a peer.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;For &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20403&quot; title=&quot;Refresh import conn on primary migration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20403&quot;&gt;LU-20403&lt;/a&gt;, ptlrpc_refresh_import_primary() can move an import to the transient NID. The reply ME then keys on that NID, but lnet_parse() stamps the reply with the restored primary. The reply does not match, and the RPC waits until it times out. The next send moves the import back. &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20403&quot; title=&quot;Refresh import conn on primary migration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20403&quot;&gt;LU-20403&lt;/a&gt; rejects a transient NID that no peer owns, but not one that the same peer owns.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Proposed fix&lt;br/&gt;
In lnet_peer_set_primary_nid(), test the -EPERM condition of lnet_peer_add_nid() before the write: a peer with LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED and no LNET_PEER_CONFIGURED in flags. Skip the write in that case. A move of the write after lnet_peer_add_nid() is not a simple change, because lnet_peer_add_nid() and lnet_peer_attach_peer_ni() read lp_primary_nid to place the primary NI.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</description>
